Source: ros-@ROS_DISTRO@-fleetless-bridge
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Andre Dehne <andre@dehne-robotik.de>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-python, python3-setuptools, python3-all
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://docs.fleetless.dev

Package: ros-@ROS_DISTRO@-fleetless-bridge
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 python3,
@ROS_DEPS@
 python3-opencv,
 python3-defusedxml,
 python3-numpy,
 python3-aiohttp,
 python3-aiortc
Description: Fleetless Bridge: connects a ROS2 robot to the Fleetless cloud
 Runs on a robot alongside its ROS2 graph, exposes configured datapoints,
 cameras and remote invocations to the Fleetless cloud, and carries the
 robot's job and asset-sync traffic. See https://docs.fleetless.dev.
 .
 Every dependency above is an ordinary apt package. `apt install` needs
 nothing beyond what this Depends: line already asks for, and installing it
 needs no network access beyond whatever the package's own mirror requires
 — it does not reach PyPI, and no maintainer script installs anything at
 configure time (see debian/postinst, which does nothing). This package
 used to run a PyPI install for three dependencies apt could not resolve;
 the last of those (python3-aiortc, replacing the LiveKit SDK) is why it
 no longer needs to.
